{
  "comment": [
    "next-layer's own settings taxonomy. Not Orca's pages, not Prusa's tabs: a page",
    "per question the print asks, ordered from the skin inwards and then out to the",
    "machine. tools/settings_layout.py turns this into src/qt/resources/settings-layout.json,",
    "which is what the app loads. Nothing here is read at run time.",
    "",
    "A rule moves a whole engine section; `keys` moves one setting out of its section,",
    "for the engine groups that mix two subjects (walls quality holds both wall and",
    "overhang settings, resolution holds both slicing and G-code output)."
  ],
